                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you are looking through the VR free-to-play tags, The Beanstalk VR experience does not hold up in 2022. Just skip it.\n\nThe Beanstalk a short 5-10 minute experience which tells a fairy tale story based off Jack and the Beanstalk. As a first student project, it's a GREAT project to use on a resume to get a job but never something you'd release as a commercial project. If I made this as a first class VR project, I'd be EXTREMELY proud of it. They did a great job on the project for 2017.\n\nIf you're a consumer and want to know why I don't recommend it, here is why:\nThe majority of the experience is only listening/waiting not interacting. You pull on a tabs of story boards to progress the experience, grab a few beans and toss them in the dirt, climb up a small portion of the beanstalk and then touch a harp. That's the The Beanstalk.",
